---
import TownHall from '../sketches/TownHall.astro';
import MarketHall from '../sketches/MarketHall.astro';
import Mersey from '../sketches/Mersey.astro';
---

<section class="section" id="stockport" aria-labelledby="stockport-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
      <span class="kicker">Look closer</span>
      <h2 id="stockport-title">Maths is all around Stockport</h2>
      <p>
        Maths isn’t only found in textbooks. It’s in the curve of the viaduct, the hands of the Town Hall clock and the
        triangles holding up the Market Hall roof. Spotting it in familiar places helps maths feel real, and a lot less
        daunting.
      </p>
    </div>
    <ul class="landmarks">
      <li class="landmark" data-reveal>
        <TownHall />
        <span class="landmark__topic">Angles and symmetry</span>
        <h3>Stockport Town Hall</h3>
        <p>At 3 o’clock the clock’s hands make a right angle, and the minute hand turns 6° every minute.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="landmark" data-reveal style="--rd:.1s">
        <MarketHall />
        <span class="landmark__topic">Triangles and structure</span>
        <h3>Stockport Market Hall</h3>
        <p>Triangles keep a roof rigid, and the three angles inside every triangle always add up to 180°.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="landmark" data-reveal style="--rd:.2s">
        <Mersey />
        <span class="landmark__topic">Distance and scale</span>
        <h3>The River Mersey</h3>
        <p>The Mersey begins in Stockport, where the Goyt and the Tame meet. On a 1 : 25 000 map, 4 cm stands for 1 km.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
